course: dictionary
lesson: 6705
title: Words that tell how something happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word oddly tells you how something is done. It means in a strange or unusual way, so it describes an action, like looking or acting. «Lately boys from both streets had started looking at Maddie oddly.» Oddly tells you how they looked: not in a normal, friendly way, but in a strange way that made Maddie notice.
explain: Oddly often comes at the start of a sentence to warn you that something is not normal. «Oddly, the door was open.» You expect a closed door, so the word makes you curious about why it is open. Oddly enough means surprisingly: «Oddly enough, the rock hyrax is a distant relative of the elephant.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «It felt powerful, then oddly lonely, because nobody passed him the ball either.» If you put in strangely, it still makes sense: it felt strangely lonely. A good check always works: if the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Oddly means in a strange or unusual way.
fact: «Oddly» often tells you that something is not normal, and it makes the reader curious.
fact: Oddly enough means surprisingly, as in «Oddly enough, the rock hyrax is a distant relative of the elephant.»
fact: You may also meet phrases like oddly shaped and oddly quiet.
fact: Oddly is an adverb, a word that tells how something is done.
exercise: «Oddly, the door was open.» What does oddly tell you? | The door was very heavy to push | *Something is not normal, and it makes you curious | The door was locked again | The door was painted a bright colour
exercise: Maddie is «looked at oddly» by the boys. What does that suggest? | In a friendly way, with big smiles | In a loud way, shouting her name | In a sleepy way, with eyes closed | *In a strange way, as if they were curious about her
exercise: Which phrase means surprisingly? | oddly lonely | *oddly enough | oddly shaped | oddly quiet
test: «It felt powerful, then oddly lonely.» Which word could replace oddly and keep the meaning? | *strangely | loudly | happily | quickly
test: The dictionary says oddly means what? | In a bored way | Very fast | *In a strange or unusual way | Happily and loudly
exam: «A wild animal that acts oddly may be sick, sometimes with rabies.» What does oddly tell you about the animal? | It is very big | It is calm and eats its food well | It has gone to sleep | *It acts in a strange, unusual way, which can be a sign of illness
